  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Botryorhodine C and the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, as it is indirectly linked through a series of targets. Botryorhodine C is predicted to interact with Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Hex-3-en-1-yl 2-methylbut-2-enoate, (1R,8S,9R,16R)-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-9-[(1R,8S,9R,16R)-4,6,12-trihydroxy-8,16-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaen-9-yl]-15-oxatetracyclo[8.6.1.02,7.014,17]heptadeca-2(7),3,5,10(17),11,13-hexaene-4,6,12-triol, and (+)-1,5-Epoxy-nor-ketoguaia-11-ene. These compounds are all predicted to target the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, indicating a possible pathway through which Botryorhodine C may influence this subunit. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, with varying scores, suggesting a plausible but not definitive relationship. The mechanism appears to involve the modulation of a key proteasome component through a series of intermediate targets, though the exact role of Botryorhodine C in this process remains to be fully elucidated.",
